HELM CHARTS - DEVOPS ENGINEER WORKFLOW

Step 1: Verify Helm Installation at the Machine level(Agent node) where execute the kubernetes is installed

wget https://get.helm.sh/helm-v3.18.6-linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar -xzf helm-v3.18.6-linux-amd64.tar.gz
sudo mv linux-amd64/helm /usr/local/bin/

helm version

Step 2: Add Helm Repository (Example: Bitnami)
"A Helm repository stores Helm charts, just like Docker Hub stores Docker images.
We use helm repo add to add a repository to our local Helm client so that we can search, download, and install pre-built applications like NGINX, MySQL, Redis, and Jenkins using Helm.

helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami  

Step 3: Update Helm Repository
helm repo update

Step 4: Search Available Charts
helm search repo nginx
helm search repo mysql

helm install my-nginx bitnami/nginx

Step 5: Create a New Helm Chart
helm create myapp

This creates the following structure:

myapp/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
├── charts/
├── templates/
│   ├── deployment.yaml
│   ├── service.yaml
│   ├── ingress.yaml
│   ├── serviceaccount.yaml
│   ├── hpa.yaml
│   └── _helpers.tpl

Step 6: Modify values.yaml

Example:
replicaCount: 2

image:
  repository: loksaieta/bankingwebapp
  tag: latest

service:
  type: ClusterIP
  port: 8080

Step 7: Modify templates if required

deployment.yaml
service.yaml
ingress.yaml
configmap.yaml
secret.yaml

Step 8: Validate Helm Chart

helm lint myapp            Checks your Helm chart for errors before deployment.   Like checking Java code with a compiler before running it.

Step 9: Generate Kubernetes YAML

helm template myapp          //helm template myapp generates the final Kubernetes YAML manifests from the Helm chart without deploying them to the Kubernetes cluster.

Step 10: Install Helm Chart

helm install banking-app ./myapp           //Deploys the Kubernetes resources (Deployment, Service, Pods, etc.) to the Kubernetes cluster.

Step 11: Verify Installation

helm list     

kubectl get all               // List all the installed resources using helm

Step 12: Upgrade Application

helm upgrade banking-app ./myapp        //Updates the existing application in Kubernetes

Step 13: Check Release Status

helm status banking-app   // helps to find the deployment status

Step 14: View Release History

helm history banking-app      //View release versions

Step 15: Rollback

helm rollback banking-app 1             //Restores the application to a previous version

Step 16: Uninstall

helm uninstall banking-app

Useful Commands:

helm version
helm repo list
helm repo update
helm search repo nginx
helm create myapp
helm lint myapp
helm template myapp
helm install banking-app ./myapp
helm list
helm status banking-app
helm upgrade banking-app ./myapp
helm history banking-app
helm rollback banking-app 1
helm uninstall banking-app

1. helm lint       → Check chart for errors
2. helm template   → Preview Kubernetes YAML
3. helm install    → Deploy application
4. helm list       → Show installed releases
5. kubectl get all → Verify Kubernetes resources
6. helm upgrade    → Update application
7. helm status     → Check deployment status
8. helm history    → View release versions
9. helm rollback   → Restore previous version
10. helm uninstall → Remove application
11. helm create   → Create Helm chart structure
12. helm template → Generate Kubernetes YAML
13. helm install  → Deploy to Kubernetes

